#~ msgid "Ampere A1 servers are popular and regions often run out. The installer tries every availability domain in your region and keeps retrying for 30 minutes. It already requests the smallest size the installer offers, 1 core and 6 GB, so there is nothing smaller to fall back to. If it gives up, run the command again later: it remembers your domain, so the command no longer needs it, and everything already created is reused. Upgrading to Pay As You Go also tends to end these errors, since paying accounts are served first when servers are scarce."
#~ msgstr ""

